Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:55:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] hip-tests: add hipGraphExecUpdate regression test for
 kernarg exhaustion

Unit_hipGraphExecUpdate_KernargPoolExhaustion builds a one-kernel graph
whose kernel writes its integer argument to device memory, exhausts
device memory with a greedy allocation loop, then repeatedly modifies
the node and calls hipGraphExecUpdate + hipGraphLaunch. Each update
captures a fresh kernel-argument slot, so the loop drives kernarg pool
growth into guaranteed allocation failure.

Pass condition: the process survives with no stale-packet value mismatch
on any iteration whose calls all reported success; any clean error code
under exhaustion is acceptable.

Validated on gfx1100 (RX 7900 XTX, ROCm 7.2.3, standalone twin of this
test): the unpatched runtime dies with SIGSEGV in libamdhip64 after
~131k update iterations (the crash in issue #10021); with the two fix
commits it completes ~121k iterations and surfaces a clean error code
with no corruption.

Related: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems/issues/10021

Signed-off-by: Tiernan de Burca <tdeburca@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
